{"name":"Sanguine","hex":"#6c110e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sanguine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of blood; blood red. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having a bodily constitution characterised by a preponderance of blood over the other bodily humours, thought to be marked by irresponsible mirth; indulgent in pleasure to the exclusion of important matters."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Blood colour; red.","Anything of a blood-red colour, as cloth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sanguine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red chalk","blocks":[{"text":"Red chalk is chalk of a reddish-brown color, which was used as a material for drawing. It is obtained from the red ochre variety of hematite. Another term for red chalk, common in older references, is sanguine. The word comes via French from the Italian sanguigna and is originally from the Latin \"sanguis\"; it refers to the color's similarity to that of dried blood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Rembrandt_van_Rijn%2C_Self-Portrait%2C_c._1637%2C_NGA_9844.jpg/330px-Rembrandt_van_Rijn%2C_Self-Portrait%2C_c._1637%2C_NGA_9844.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_chalk","wikidata":"Q901944"},{"title":"Four temperaments","blocks":[{"text":"The four temperament theory is a proto-psychological theory which suggests that there are four fundamental personality types: sanguine, choleric, melancholic, and phlegmatic. Most formulations include the possibility of mixtures among the types where an individual's personality types overlap and they share two or more temperaments. Greek physician Hippocrates described the four temperaments as part of the ancient medical concept of humourism, which states that four bodily fluids affect human personality traits and behaviours. Modern medical science does not define a fixed relationship between internal secretions and personality, although some psychological personality type systems use categories similar to the Greek temperaments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Lavater1792.jpg/330px-Lavater1792.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_temperaments","wikidata":"Q638210"},{"title":"Sanguine (tincture)","blocks":[{"text":"Sanguine is a stain, or non-standard tincture in heraldry, of a blood-red colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Clayhills_COA.svg/330px-Clayhills_COA.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanguine_(tincture)","wikidata":"Q218177"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/120px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/250px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/120px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/L%27Image_et_le_Pouvoir_-_Etude_d%27apr%C3%A8s_un_buste_romain.jpg/120px-L%27Image_et_le_Pouvoir_-_Etude_d%27apr%C3%A8s_un_buste_romain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb